"""
Modifications made for use with MSI 16-JULY-2026
"""
"""
 ThInK V 1.0 Model
 Theoretically Informed Kinetics (ThInK): Establishing a modern C0-C3 mechanism for combustion modeling
 Stephen J. Klippenstein*, Raghu Sivaramakrishnan*, David H. Bross, Michael P. Burke, Sarah N. Elliott, Peter Glarborg, C. Franklin Goldsmith, Nils Hansen,
 Ahren W. Jasper, Nicole J. Labbe, Clayton R. Mulvihill, Branko Ruscic, Yujie Tao, Judit Zador, James A. Miller
 160 species, 1089 reactions 20-May-2022 IDENTIFIED DUPLICATES FROM 10-MAY CORRECTED WITH JZ HELP
 160 species, 1104 reactions 11-May-2022
 156 species, 1050 reactions
RS comments 20-April-2021
H+CH3(+M) updated to best fit as per 2019 email to JAM
C2H2+C2H2 only in one direction with JZ input
RS Comments 5-April-2021
Colliders for H+H+M moved from below R2 to below R1
OCO replaced by CO2
HCOH replaced by CHOH
HOCHO replaced by OCHOH
DH commented out for CH3+OH=CH2+H2O and in some other places
No Arrhenius parameters for C2H5+CH3OO=C2H5O+CH3O, hence commented out
OCHCO replaced by OCCHO (GLYOXAL RADICAL)
OCHCHO+H=CH2O+HCO is a duplicate reaction JAM estimate commented out, Friedrichs left in
CH3CHCH+H=CH2CHCH2+H typo in !PLOG pressures 1.00E+02 replaced by 1.00E+00
DUPLICATES IDENTIFIED 10-MAY-2022
968 AND 976; 969 AND 984; 977 AND 985; 970 AND 992;978 AND 993;986 AND 994;971 AND 1000;979 AND 1001; 987 AND 1002; 995 AND 1003; 972 AND 1008; 980 AND 1009
998 AND 1O10; 996 AND 1011; 1004 AND 1012; 989 AND 1016; 981 AND 1017; 989 AND 1018; 997 AND 1019; 1020 AND 1005; 1013 AND 1021; 1035 AND 1023; 973 AND 1036
 Journal Abbreviations
 APJ = Astro. Phys. J.
 BBPC = Berichte Bunsenges. Phys. Chem.
 CF = Combust. Flame
 CPL = Chem. Phys. Lett.
 CST = Combust. Sci. Tech.
 EF = Energy Fuels
 IJCK = Int. J. Chem. Kinet.
 JCC = J. Comp. Chem.
 JCP = J. Chem. Phys.
 JCSFT = J. Chem. Soc. Faraday Trans.
 JGR = J. Geophys. Res.
 JPC = J. Phys. Chem.
 JPCA = J. Phys. Chem. A
 JPCL = J. Phys. Chem. Lett.
 JPCRD = J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data
 JPPA = J. Photochem. Photobio. A
 NC = Nature Chem.
 PCCP = Phys. Chem. Chem. Phys.
 PCI = Proc. Combust. Inst. (including the earlier Int. Symp. Comb.)
 TCA = Theor. Chem. Acc.
 ZPC = Zeit. Phys. Chem.

 The first line in the PLOG expressions is meant to reproduce the 1 atm rate constant to the
 extent possible with a single modified Arrhenius expression.

"""

units(length='cm', time='s', quantity='mol', act_energy='cal/mol')

ideal_gas(name='gas',
          elements="H O N Ar He Kr",
          species="""AR                KR                HE
                     N2                H                 H2
                     O                 OH                H2O
                     O2                HO2               H2O2
                     OX                O2X               OH*
                     O3                HOOOOH
                     """,
          reactions='all',
          transport='Mix',
          initial_state=state(temperature=300.0, pressure=OneAtm))

